        "title": "chore(deps): refresh package and pnpm pins",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- refresh all policy-eligible direct development dependencies and resolved transitives\n- update pnpm to 11.13.0 in package metadata and the AWS image builder\n- keep credentialed manual AWS workflow actions unchanged until a disposable live workflow path is available\n\n## Freshness policy\n\nThe repository's 48-hour minimum release age remains enforced. The package set is fully current under that policy. pnpm 11.13.1, AWS SDK 3.1088.0, and Workers Types 5.20260716.1 are intentionally held because they are too fresh.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`\n- `pnpm check`\n  - 157 Node tests passed\n  - 20 Worker tests passed\n  - 53 AWS tests passed; 4 PostgreSQL integration tests skipped without a configured isolated database\n- `pnpm audit --audit-level low`: no known vulnerabilities\n- Linux/AMD64 AWS image build on Node 22.23.1; runtime bundle import passed as non-root `node`\n- source-blind local console/API contract: root 200 HTML, stable state, invalid create 422 without mutation, unknown route 404\n- AutoReview on the full branch against `origin/main`: clean\n\nNo deployment, image publication, release, version bump, tag, registry publish, or GitHub Release is part of this PR.\n",
